  "worked_solution": "Notice that the coefficient of $p$ in the first equation is $4,$ and the coefficient of $p$ in the second equation is $-4.$ \n\nSince these numbers add to zero, we can add the two equations, *eliminate* the variable $p,$ and solve the resulting equation for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{4p}+q & =-24 \\\\ -\\cancel{4p}+7q & =24 \\\\ (q+7q) & =(-24+24) \\\\ 8q & =0 \\\\ q & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $q=0.$ However, we still need to find $p.$ To do this, we substitute $q=0$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p+q & =-24 \\\\ 4p+(0) & =-24 \\\\ 4p & =-24 \\\\ p & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=-6,\\,q=0,$ which can be expressed as $(\\,-\\,6,0\\,).$",
